From e3c363fb45a6b022dab9a3a5eb3bd4fd8a1b0140 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 23:12:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] nvk/rm: dma-buf export and import through nvidia-drm,
 DRM format modifiers

Zero-copy presentation for the RM backend.  RM memory becomes a dma-buf
the way NVIDIA's own userspace does it: the memory object is exported to
a fresh /dev/nvidiactl descriptor (NV0000_CTRL_CMD_OS_UNIX_EXPORT_OBJECT_TO_FD),
nvidia-drm imports that descriptor as a GEM object
(DRM_NVIDIA_GEM_IMPORT_NVKMS_MEMORY, with the NVKMS surface parameters of
the image the memory was allocated for) and PRIME makes the dma-buf.
Import is the reverse: PRIME_FD_TO_HANDLE, DRM_NVIDIA_GEM_EXPORT_NVKMS_MEMORY
to a /dev/nvidiactl descriptor, NV0000_CTRL_CMD_OS_UNIX_IMPORT_OBJECT_FROM_FD
into our client under a handle from crm_new_handle, placement from
NV0041_CTRL_CMD_GET_SURFACE_INFO.

Under Conduit the DRM node is the guest's nvidia-drm stand-in, which
forwards both GEM ioctls to the host's nvidia-drm and puts a guest GEM
object in front of the host's, so Xwayland, the compositor (NVIDIA's EGL
and GBM) and Conduit's scanout to the host all use the VRAM NVK rendered
into.

- pdev: find the nvidia-drm node at the GPU's PCI address (Conduit's PCI
  mirror, which is also what RM reports), check DRM_IOCTL_VERSION and
  DRM_NVIDIA_GET_DEV_INFO, fill drm.render_dev/primary_dev (so the WSI
  sees the same device as the X server and the compositor), and set
  has_dma_buf.  NVK_RM_DMABUF=0 turns it off.  has_alloc_tiled is set:
  kinds are applied per mapping as before, a tiled allocation just
  records the layout; this enables VK_EXT_image_drm_format_modifier with
  NIL's NVIDIA block-linear modifiers, which match what nvidia-drm
  reports for GB202 (generic kind 0x06, kind generation 2, sector layout
  1, e.g. 0x0300000000606015).
- dev: its own open of the node for GEM handles.
- mem: one GEM object per memory, made on first export (every export is
  then the same dma-buf); shared system memory is RM's NV01_MEMORY_SYSTEM,
  never our own pages, which another client cannot use.
- sync: drop vk_sync_binary's emulated sync_file import/export.  The WSI
  took it for real sync_file support and the first vkAcquireNextImageKHR
  failed with VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE; without it the WSI asks
  for implicit sync and waits before presenting (wait_before_present).
- nvrm_api.h: the OS_UNIX export/import controls, GET_SURFACE_INFO and the
  nvidia-drm/NVKMS structures, with size checks.
- lib: crm_new_handle/crm_release_handle (optional).

On an RTX 5090 in a Conduit guest (GNOME 50, Xwayland): vkcube renders
through the native X11 and Wayland WSI paths with no CPU copy; at
1920x1080 with uncapped present modes, 2900 fps on X11 (software WSI:
630) and 4900 fps on Wayland (software: 590).
